# {{ mosaics.title }}

One item per year, each carrying {{ n_assets }} single-band analysis rasters on
ETRS89-LAEA (EPSG:3035) at {{ analysis_grid.resolution | int }} m, plus {{ n_viz }} PMTiles archives
for drawing them, beside the rasters in the same item directory. Agents: read
[`AGENTS.md`]({{ page_base }}/mosaics/AGENTS.md).

The grid has two deliberate properties:

- **It is equal-area.** A pixel covers the same {{ (analysis_grid.resolution ** 2) | int }} m² everywhere, so a
  glacier area or an area change is a pixel count.
- **It is the same every year.** The extent is a fixed constant, so every year
  has identical `proj:shape` and `proj:transform`.

Use the COGs for analysis. The collection's `renders` block defines display
ranges, color ramps and decibel conversions for clients that support them.

## Building a cube

```python
import odc.stac
import pystac

collection = pystac.Collection.from_file(
    "{{ public_base }}/mosaics/collection.json"
)
cube = odc.stac.load(
    list(collection.get_items(recursive=True)),
    bands=["coh12_vv", "rtc_vv"],
    chunks={},
)
```

Every year shares one grid, so the years form a time axis directly.

## PMTiles for web maps

Each year's item also holds PMTiles archives for web maps, beside the COGs.
The `_viz` suffix marks them as visualization products. They are tiled on
WebMercatorQuad up to zoom {{ max_zoom }}, resampled from the MGRS tiles.

The archive pixels hold encoded values: an 8-bit code in all three channels of
a lossy WebP tile, linear over a fixed range per layer. Backscatter and
composite quality maps are encoded in decibels; coherence is linear. Each
archive's asset declares the decoding as `raster:scale` and `raster:offset`.

Each year's style declares every archive as a MapLibre `raster-dem` source
with a custom encoding and draws it as a `color-relief` layer, with a default
ramp from the [Scientific colour maps](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1243862)
([Crameri et al., 2020](https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-020-19160-7)). A client
can change the ramp and the range without re-tiling.

Each year's style sits beside its archives, at `{year}/styles/default.json`,
and the collection's style draws the latest year.

**To draw a map**, load a year's style in MapLibre GL JS, which decodes custom
`raster-dem` encodings. The style names its archives relative to itself, as
Portolan styles do, while MapLibre and the PMTiles protocol resolve a source URL
against the page, so resolve them against the style first:

```js
const protocol = new pmtiles.Protocol();
maplibregl.addProtocol("pmtiles", protocol.tile);

const styleUrl = "{{ public_base }}/mosaics/{{ last_year }}/styles/default.json";
const style = await (await fetch(styleUrl)).json();
for (const source of Object.values(style.sources)) {
  const path = source.url.replace("pmtiles://", "");
  source.url = "pmtiles://" + new URL(path, styleUrl).href;
}
new maplibregl.Map({ container: "map", style });
```

